      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A \"patriotic\" history curriculum is a powerful tool for building community and instilling civic duty, but it often fails to prepare students for the complex realities of modern society if it glosses over systemic issues. True intellectual growth comes from engaging with uncomfortable truths, including the history of racism and power struggles, because ignoring them only creates a fragile foundation for democracy. You cannot teach kids to be critical thinkers by sanitizing history; instead, a robust education must balance national pride with an honest examination of our flaws to foster genuine resilience and informed citizenship.",
